.nh
.TH "PB-RECORDINGS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-recordings - List and replay terminal recordings


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb recordings [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List, replay and export terminal recordings, and start or stop recording a session you are
attached to. Team recordings are made on the recorded machine and stay there, encrypted for the
team; the team's bucket can hold an archived copy. Replay and export are audited by Paperboat
before any data moves, travel over the end-to-end encrypted machine connection, and are
decrypted on your computer with your unlocked ENV vault (pb env unlock).

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for recordings


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb recordings list
  pb recordings play rec_abc123 --speed 2
  pb recordings export rec_abc123 -o session.cast
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-recordings-export(1)\fP, \fBpb-recordings-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-recordings-play(1)\fP, \fBpb-recordings-start(1)\fP, \fBpb-recordings-stop(1)\fP
